                Unit = null,
                Description = "This indicator related to SDG 10.3.1/16.b.1 Proportion of population reporting having personally felt discriminated against or harassed in the previous 12 months on the basis of a ground of discrimination prohibited under international human rights law. Cross reference: SDG 5.1.1; SDG 10.7.4.In order to accelerate anticorruption synergy, the government has issued Presidential Regulation No. 54 of 2018 concerning the National Strategy for Corruption Prevention(Perpres Stranas PK 2018). Perpres Stranas PK 2018 is a national policy direction that contains focus and targets on corruption prevention which are used as a reference for ministries, institutions, local governments and other stakeholders in implementingcorruption prevention in Indonesia.In addition, in Presidential Regulation No. 59 of 2017 concerning the implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals, corruption is one of the global goals, where the global goal is to substantially reduce corruption and bribery in all its forms.Even in the 2020-2024 National Midterm Development Plan (RPJMN), it was stated that the national target to be realized was to increase the Anti-Corruption Behavior Index(IPAK) to 4.14 in 2024SPAK measures the community's permissiveness to corrupt behavior, socialization andanti-corruption knowledge. Based on SPAK, Anti-Corruption Behavior Index (IPAK) is formed based on two dimensions, that are perception and experience. In this regard, IPAK will be analyzed in terms of public perception and also in terms of community experience when using or interacting with public services and other experiences.",
